A vendored repository. `go mod vendor` copies no go.mod files, so a walk finds one
module here and the count is honest either way — what this pins is that ./... omits
the vendored package, so the package set is smaller than the directory tree suggests.
Legacy vendor trees from dep or glide did carry go.mod files, which is why discovery
skips vendor regardless.

modules_on_disk: 1
go_list_m: 1
go_list_dotdotdot: 1
-- go.mod --
module fixture.test/vendored

go 1.27

require fixture.test/dep v1.0.0
-- app/app.go --
package app

import "fixture.test/dep"

func A() int { return dep.D() }
-- vendor/modules.txt --
# fixture.test/dep v1.0.0
## explicit; go 1.27
fixture.test/dep
-- vendor/fixture.test/dep/dep.go --
package dep

func D() int { return 9 }
